UniXNU 3fd6a3c: catalog entry Adreno650 (xVanTuring/Adreno650, the SM8250 branch of Adreno740), gap G3 of macOS-Pad-6

Format 2 selects drivers through components.toml, and the A650 fork had no entry, so a board could carry it only as a
retained --local-module source and could not name it in [components] include. The entry pins the fork at 01db67e0,
depends on the kits the pipa recipe links (AdrenoPM4, AdrenoFirmware, ArmSmmu4K; not Sm8550Platform: the A650 build
leaves sheng's GMU platform, config and service out and uses the board package's A650 cold start instead), and builds
with the device script build-adreno650.py (devices/pipa/scripts, the recipe of UniXNU-pipa format 1), whose archive is
build/adreno650/libAdreno650.a. os_abi: the iPadOS 17 profile it ran under, and macOS 26.5, against whose xnu-12377
kernel macOS-Pad-6's kernel step compiles and links it (arm64e, kernel-build attempts 17-18; with libPipaGpu.a for
the hand-off and export symbols). verified_devices stays empty: no GPU result exists for macOS.

Applied by macOS-Pad-6's scripts/pipa_unixnu.py to its UniXNU copy and meant as the upstream proposal. Resolution
tested on the host (pipa_unixnu.py check, tests/test_unixnu_patches.py); the driver was not built.

